Let's determine how many pages Solo needs to read on average each day to complete his reading within the remaining 4 days.

**Step 1: Calculate the Total Number of Pages to Read**

\[
\begin{align*}
\text{Science} & = 4 \text{ pages} \\
\text{Social Studies} & = 20 \text{ pages} \\
\text{History} & = 7 \text{ pages} \\
\text{Geography} & = 8 \text{ pages} \\
\hline
\text{Total Pages} & = 4 + 20 + 7 + 8 = 39 \text{ pages}
\end{align*}
\]

**Step 2: Subtract the Pages Already Read**

\[
\begin{align*}
\text{Pages Read on Monday} & = 15 \text{ pages} \\
\text{Pages Remaining} & = 39 - 15 = 24 \text{ pages}
\end{align*}
\]

**Step 3: Determine the Average Pages to Read Each Day**

\[
\begin{align*}
\text{Number of Days Remaining} & = 4 \text{ days} \\
\text{Average Pages per Day} & = \frac{24 \text{ pages}}{4 \text{ days}} = 6 \text{ pages/day}
\end{align*}
\]

**Final Answer:**

\[
\boxed{6}
\]
